                <pb facs="0168" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4624: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Personal Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-16T18:00:00-05:00">January 16, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. My telegram No. 26, January 16, 1 p.m. The Mendieta group has divided as to
                    whether or not to follow Mendieta’s lead in supporting Hevia, the majority of
                    the group this morning being in opposition to their chief. However, Hevia is
                    still making serious efforts to secure the support of the entire group.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
